{"seq":2,"slug":"designing-agent-friendly-tools","title":"Designing Agent Friendly Tools","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/agent-ready-apis-and-tools/designing-agent-friendly-tools","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"clear-purpose-and-naming","title":"清晰的用途与命名","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/agent-ready-apis-and-tools/designing-agent-friendly-tools/clear-purpose-and-naming","wordCount":2350,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"inputs-outputs-and-schemas","title":"输入输出与模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/agent-ready-apis-and-tools/designing-agent-friendly-tools/inputs-outputs-and-schemas","wordCount":2001,"readingTime":9},{"seq":3,"slug":"errors-as-guidance","title":"把错误设计成指引","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/agent-ready-apis-and-tools/designing-agent-friendly-tools/errors-as-guidance","wordCount":1962,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲具体怎么设计一个 agent 用得好的工具:清晰的用途与命名——让 agent 一眼看懂这个工具做什么、什么时候该用它;输入输出与模式——用明确的 schema 约束参数、用结构化且适量的返回让 agent 好填好用;以及把错误设计成指引——错误不只是报告失败,更要告诉 agent「哪里错了、怎么改」,让它能自我纠正而非卡死。\n"}